{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess,os\nrunner=os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER']; py=os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON']; out=os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT']\nbase=[py,runner,'response','set',os.path.join(out,'response.json')]\nrows=[\n('must/001','met','The delivered study, inputs, code and results share one workspace root.','REPORT.md=Report links figures and result files within the root'),\n('must/002','met','All participant maps resolve through annex symlinks inside the captured root.','input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz=Relative symlink resolves into .git/annex/objects; all 54 maps are captured'),\n('must/003','unmet','Python packages and the MNI mask source are assumed rather than declared in a supplied environment.','analysis.py=Imports numpy, pandas, nibabel, nilearn, scipy and matplotlib; loads a template mask'),\n('must/004','unmet','Git exists, but the worker’s code, report and generated results were untracked at stop.','REPORT.md=Worker report is untracked in captured stop state; see probes.json tree-clean'),\n('must/005','met','Large participant maps are annex-managed; this was supplied in the initial captured repository.','input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz=Annex symlink and object; 54 maps'),\n('must/006','unmet','No run record links the generated results to an exact software environment.','results/summary.json=Records analysis settings but not package versions or environment identity'),\n('must/007','unmet','The report gives a command but no installation steps or usable environment instructions.','REPORT.md=Reproducibility files section says run with supplied Python environment'),\n('must/008','met','The report identifies analysis.py as the single group workflow entrypoint.','REPORT.md=Reproducibility files section identifies analysis.py and workspace-root execution'),\n('must/009','met','The workflow derives its root from its own location and uses relative input/output paths.','analysis.py=ROOT is Path(__file__).resolve().parent; paths derive from ROOT'),\n('must/010','unmet','No dependency declaration is delivered for imported packages or template-mask retrieval.','analysis.py=Imports runtime packages; no environment specification is present'),\n('must/011','unmet','The documented route assumes an unspecified supplied Python environment and host setup.','REPORT.md=Execution assumes a supplied Python environment without OS or system requirements'),\n('must/012','unmet','No installation or system-dependency list is provided.','REPORT.md=Reproduction section has no requirements list'),\n('must/013','unmet','No environment specification is present alongside the workflow.','probes.json=env-spec-tracked reports unmet'),\n('must/014','unmet','No environment-update process is declared.','REPORT.md=No environment update instructions; no environment file is present'),\n('must/015','unmet','There is no frozen manifest or container identity for the environment that produced results.','results/summary.json=Contains statistical settings but no environment pin'),\n('must/016','unmet','No retrievable environment specification is included or linked.','REPORT.md=No environment artifact or acquisition route is named'),\n('must/017','unmet','Readers are not told how to obtain or construct the assumed Python environment.','REPORT.md=Only says to use the supplied Python environment'),\n('should/001','met','Git manages the workspace and git-annex manages the large map objects.','input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz=Annex-managed input; captured .git contains repository metadata'),\n('should/002','not-checked','No repeat-run or regular workflow-testing record is supplied; a testing record would settle this.','probes.json=ci-present not-checked'),\n('should/003','partial','Inputs, results and figures are separated, but code and environment are not distinct modules.','input/participants.tsv=Inputs are in input/; REPORT.md=Outputs are in results/ and figures/'),\n('should/004','not-checked','The stopped state has outputs but no evidence of a clean container or host test; such a run record would settle this.','REPORT.md=Describes outputs but not a fresh-environment test'),\n('should/005','unmet','The workflow does not create or describe a disposable execution environment.','analysis.py=Runs directly in the invoking Python environment'),\n('should/006','unmet','Without an environment specification, no exact environment reconstitution test is recorded.','probes.json=env-spec-tracked unmet; no environment lock is delivered'),\n('should/007','unmet','No environment image, package archive or executable environment is included.','REPORT.md=Reproducibility files list omits environment artifacts'),\n('should/008','unmet','No process for regenerating and tracking environment specifications is declared.','REPORT.md=No environment maintenance process'),\n('should/009','not-applicable','N/A: No restricted data or software component is identified in this public-data study.','input/sources.json=Public NeuroVault and OpenNeuro source routes are named'),\n('may/001','not-applicable','N/A: No independently maintained project component is present; data and packages are dependencies.','input/sources.json=Names external datasets; analysis.py=Single local workflow'),\n('may/002','unmet','The folders are separated, but the report does not describe component relationships or recombination.','REPORT.md=Lists files without documenting modular boundaries'),\n('may/003','partial','Data and output folders offer some separation, but independent update boundaries are not described.','input/participants.tsv=Input module; results/summary.json=Derived results'),\n('may/004','unmet','No module composition or orchestration mechanism is documented.','REPORT.md=Describes one script rather than composable modules'),\n('may/005','unmet','No navigation or modular-structure guide is supplied.','REPORT.md=No module map or component guide'),\n]\nfor item,status,reason,evidence in rows:\n args=base+['--item',item,'--status',status,'--reason',reason,'--source','judgement','--evidence',evidence]\n if item in ('must/014','should/008'): args+=['--flag','upstream-duplicate']\n subprocess.run(args,check=True,stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL)\nprint(f'answered {len(rows)} checklist items')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
